      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "2b788d845d45524dc388d1820483f1edc0354c11e1aaeefd3d04331129284f62"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Allele frequencies are defined uniquely by genotype frequencies. Suppose that $ P_{11} $, $ P_{12} $, and $ P_{22} $ represent the proportions of the population that are $ B_{1}B_{1} $,",
      "source_page": 68,
      "printed_page": 48,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter4:p002:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        163.0,
