    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, the general rule for a diploid, autosomal locus is that the frequency of an allele is estimated by the observed frequency of homozygotes plus one-half the observed frequency of all heterozygotes containing that allele.",
      "source_page": 69,
      "printed_page": 49,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter4:p003:b5"
      ],
      "bbox": [
